course: dictionary
lesson: 2837
title: Dizzy: spinning, high or silly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Dizzy» usually means your head feels like it is spinning and you might fall over. The words around it give the clues, so read the whole sentence before you choose a meaning.
explain: «A boy in Arizona played football all afternoon in the heat without drinking; he got dizzy, his head pounded and he fainted.» Hot weather, no water, a pounding head and fainting are the clues. Dizzy means feeling faint and spinning here, not silly.
explain: Dizzy can also describe something very high, as in «dizzy heights». Informally, a dizzy person is silly or forgetful. Test your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: If you feel dizzy, sit down, drink some water and tell an adult. After a bump on the head, get help.
fact: Dizzy means feeling as if everything is spinning and you might fall over.
fact: «Dizzy heights» means very high places.
fact: Informally, a dizzy person is silly or forgetful.
fact: In your inner ear, a fluid keeps moving for a moment after you stop spinning, which is one reason you can feel dizzy.
fact: You can feel dizzy from heat, not drinking enough water, standing up too fast or hitting your head. Sit down, drink water and tell an adult.
exercise: «A boy in Arizona... he got dizzy, his head pounded and he fainted.» What does dizzy mean here? | Hungry | Very high up | Silly and forgetful | *Feeling as if everything is spinning
exercise: The climbers stood at the dizzy heights of the mountain. What does dizzy mean here? | *Very high | Very silly | Very wet | Very cold
exercise: Ben says his sister is dizzy because she forgot her shoes again. What does dizzy mean in his sentence? | Very high up | Feeling as if the room is spinning | *Silly or forgetful | Very hot
test: «After the spin on the playground, Aisha felt dizzy and had to sit down.» What should Aisha do? | Laugh and ignore it | Run straight back to the swings | Stand up very fast | *Sit down, drink water and tell an adult
test: «Heat exhaustion can make a person feel weak, dizzy and sick.» What does dizzy mean here? | Very high | Silly | Very happy | *Feeling as if everything is spinning
exam: «A boy in Scotland ate shiny red berries from a bush in the park; he was sick and dizzy, and his mum had to rush him to hospital.» What is the best meaning of dizzy? | *Feeling as if everything is spinning and you might fall over | Very high up | Forgetful | Hungry
